    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac12$",
      "worked": "Let the semicircle have radius $R$ and the inscribed circle have radius $r$. The inner centre is $r$ above the diameter. At the upper tangency, $R=r+r$, so $r=\\frac{R}{2}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{A_{\\text{circle}}}{A_{\\text{semicircle}}}&=\\frac{\\pi(R/2)^2}{\\tfrac12\\pi R^2}\\\\\\frac{A_{\\text{circle}}}{A_{\\text{semicircle}}}&=\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 43
  },
